From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:03:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 17/22] Markdown preview: inline images, README HTML, details,
 alerts, footnotes

The iced Markdown widget drops block HTML and draws every image as a
block that swallows the paragraph text before it, so GitHub READMEs
(badge rows, centred logos, <details>) render poorly.

One pass over the pulldown-cmark events now splits the document: plain
Markdown still goes to the widget, while paragraphs with images, HTML
blocks, GFM alerts and footnotes are drawn by the preview:

- images in a paragraph stay inline and wrap; linked images keep the
  link, clicks go through the existing link rules
- align="center" on p/div centres, <img> keeps width/height, <br>,
  <details>/<summary> is a per-tab expander, closed by default
- other tags are stripped and their text kept; comments are hidden
- > [!NOTE] and friends become callouts with a theme coloured bar
- footnote references become superscript numbers, bodies a list at
  the end

Remote images are never fetched: they show as a badge-size chip with
the alt text. Documents without HTML, images, footnotes or alerts go to
the widget whole, as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

